# Note: This code is purely AI-generated.
# 56 of the warnings in a single build came from these two probes. They iterate a platform-wide
# partition list (product, system_ext, vendor_dlkm, odm_dlkm, system_dlkm ...) and every boot-partition
# name (boot, init_boot) regardless of what the device actually has, and warned for each miss - twice
# per partition plus once for the empty result. That is not a defect report, it is the tool describing
# its own fixed probe list, and it buried the real findings in the same log.
#
# The fix keeps the warnings meaningful: probe only paths that exist in the input, and warn only when
# the partition IS part of this build but carries no build.prop - a genuine anomaly. A new
# DoesInputFileContainPartition() helper distinguishes the two cases. Verified against the target-files
# tree: this device has SYSTEM, VENDOR, ODM and SYSTEM/{product,system_ext}; it has no *_dlkm
# partitions, which is why those five warned.
